</ul>

<h2>5. Cancelling</h2>
<p>You can cancel at any time from the <a href="{{ site.app }}/portal">customer portal</a>, with no penalty and no notice period. Cancellation takes effect at the end of the period you have already paid for, and your cloud server keeps running until then. We do not refund the remaining part of a period, because you keep your access for all of it.</p>

<h2>6. Your data</h2>
<p>The accounting data you put into your cloud server is yours. You can download all of it at any time, and we suggest you do so before you cancel or delete anything.</p>
<p>We access the contents of your server only where it is needed to run and maintain the service, to help you with support you have asked for, to provide a copy to the payer as described below, or where the law requires it.</p>
<p>If someone other than you pays for the subscription, we may give that person or organisation a copy of the data on the cloud server once we have verified that they are the payer. We will email the address on the account when we do. Your own access and data are not affected.</p>
<p>When a subscription ends — by cancellation, non-payment, or a trial that was not converted — the cloud server is stopped and its data may be deleted. We do not commit to keeping it for any particular length of time, so download your data first. Deleting a cloud server in the customer portal removes it and its data straight away.</p>

<h2>7. Advisors</h2>
<p>An advisor is an independent accountant or bookkeeper, listed in our <a href="/advisors/">advisor directory</a>, who can be attached to your cloud server. Advisors are not our employees or agents. We don't vet their work, we are not responsible for the advice or services they give you, and anything you agree with an advisor — including any fees they charge for their own work — is between you and them.</p>
<p>An advisor becomes attached to your cloud server if you sign up through their referral link, if you choose one in the <a href="{{ site.app }}/portal">customer portal</a>, or if they add you using the email address and site address of your account. While attached, an advisor can see your cloud server's address, the email on the account, your plan and renewal date, and your payment history — not the accounting data inside your server. You can see who is attached, and remove them, under Your Advisor in the customer portal at any time.</p>
<p>We may pay an advisor a commission on what you pay us. The price of your subscription is the same whether or not an advisor is attached, and attaching or removing one does not change what you are charged.</p>

